course: dictionary
lesson: 9395
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning an author means by reading the words around it. The dictionary gives sprinkler two meanings: a device that sprays water over grass or plants, and a device on a ceiling that sprays water automatically when there is a fire.
explain: «It doesn't run backwards, because wet grass can also come from a sprinkler, dew or a dog.» Here sprinkler means the garden device, because it wets grass, just as dew and dogs do. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: The topic often gives the clue. In a school or a shop, a sprinkler is usually a fire safety device fixed to the ceiling. In a garden on a hot day, it is the thing children run through. A sprinkler system is a set of sprinklers working together.
fact: A sprinkler is a device, a machine or fitting that does a job.
fact: Garden sprinklers spray water over grass or plants.
fact: Fire sprinklers are fixed to ceilings and spray water by themselves when there is a fire.
fact: «Little Enceladus is like a garden sprinkler made of ice»: the comparison helps you picture its water jets, which feed one of Saturn's rings.
fact: Sprinkler is a noun, so one is a sprinkler and more than one are sprinklers.
exercise: «The children ran through the garden sprinkler on the hot day.» What is a sprinkler here? | A bird that sings in the morning | *A device that sprays water over grass | A fire alarm on the wall | A long hose for washing cars
exercise: «The sprinkler on the ceiling burst into spray when the smoke rose.» What does sprinkler mean here? | A sort of watering can | *A device on a ceiling that sprays water when there is a fire | A device that sprays water over grass or plants | A fire engine with a long ladder
exercise: What is the plural of sprinkler? | sprinklerings | sprinkles | *sprinklers | sprinkler's
test: «Sprinklers, dew and dogs wet grass too.» Which of these can wet grass, according to the sentence? | Only rain and snow | *A sprinkler, dew or a dog | Only fire sprinklers in a school | A fire alarm or a light bulb
test: In a school or shop, what does a sprinkler on the ceiling do? | Rings a loud bell to warn everyone | Turns the lights on when it gets dark | *Sprays water by itself when there is a fire | Sprays water over the grass in the playground
exam: «The sprinkler in the ceiling went off and soaked the whole shop floor.» Which meaning fits? | A device that sprays water over grass or plants | A jet of ice from a far-off moon | *A device on a ceiling that sprays water when there is a fire | A kind of hose for cars
